# permissions.meridian
# Flat-path regression coverage for the Phase-8 rule desugar (top-of-file
# rules, no headings). The same rule shapes now express in-section inside
# corpora/governance/skills/*.meri (grantaccess.meri, reviewrequests.meri,
# escalatepending.meri) — this fixture keeps the original flat path exercised
# too. See docs/13_SKILL_MD_PORTING.md and AGENTS.md §6 pitfall #15.

# Rules

A user with clearance "denied" must not access classified resources.

A user with role admin may access classified resources.

A reviewer may approve access requests whose queue position is at most 3.

An access request for a classified resource must be approved by a security officer before the grant.

When an access request is flagged as overdue, escalate the access request.

# Workflows

To let a user access a resource:
  invoke access.grant with user = the user, resource = the resource.

To have a reviewer approve an access request:
  invoke audit.log with request = the access request.

To grant an access request for a resource:
  invoke access.grant with user = the access request's requestor, resource = the resource.

To escalate an overdue access request:
  invoke audit.log with request = the access request.
